# The .editorconfig sets end_of_line = lf, and IDE0055 enforces it at build time.
# Without this file, git checks files out with CRLF on Windows, so a Windows
# contributor's very first build fails on formatting in files they never touched.
# Normalising to LF in the working tree on every platform makes the rule
# satisfiable everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched. `* text=auto` above would otherwise leave
# these to git's NUL-byte heuristic, and a test fixture that gets line-ending
# normalised is a test fixture that no longer parses.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.epub binary
*.mobi binary
*.azw binary
*.azw3 binary
*.prc binary
*.djvu binary
*.djv binary
*.doc binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
*.eml binary
*.db binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary
